title: Calling Out the Factories
subtitle: The big plants of Berlin are holding meetings.
view-if: crisis_january = 1 and jan_strike_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; jan_strike_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Calling Out the Factories

At Schwartzkopff, AEG and Siemens the workers are meeting in the yards. Some want a general strike until Ebert goes. Others pass resolutions against "the fratricide" and ask all three socialist parties to make peace.

- @general: Call a general strike.
- @unity: Take up the call for workers' unity.

@general
subtitle: If the railways and the power stations stop, Noske's volunteers will be slow to arrive.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_noske = Math.max(1, Q.e19_noske - 2);
Q.repression += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Noske\'s volunteers: ' + Q.e19_noske + ',000';
!}

The trams stop. At the Moabit power station the strikers and the engineers argue shift by shift. Noske's trains from Zossen wait in the sidings.

@unity
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The factories will listen to us. The Independents may then speak for us to the government.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any truce with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.e19_talks = 1;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Our speakers support the unity resolutions. In the plants we gain a hearing. In the newspaper district we lose friends.
